# Matmul over oneDNN's CI shapes (shapes_2d_ci: DLRM, NCF, RNN-T; shapes_2d,
# shapes_3d) on the rv64 GEMM (jit:rvv): every data-type path, the weights
# left to the primitive (pre-packed panels) against row- and column-major
# user weights, and the attributes the f32 path takes.

# Every data-type path
--reset
--dt=f32,f16:f16:f16,bf16:bf16:bf16,s8:s8:s32
--stag=abx --dtag=abx
--wtag=any,abx,ba
--batch=shapes_2d_ci
--batch=shapes_2d
--wtag=any,abx,acb
--batch=shapes_3d

# The other int8 source and destination types
--reset
--dt=u8:s8:s32,u8:s8:f32,s8:s8:s8
--stag=abx --dtag=abx
--wtag=any,abx,ba
--batch=shapes_2d_ci

# f32 with a bias (one value per N) and post-ops
--reset
--dt=f32
--stag=abx --dtag=abx
--wtag=any,abx,ba
--bia-dt=f32 --bia_mask=2
--attr-post-ops=,relu,add:f32:per_oc
--batch=shapes_2d_ci
